<title>CHINA: China trade surplus $10.29 bln in January-April.</title>
<headline>China trade surplus $10.29 bln in January-April.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>China posted a trade surplus of $10.29 billion for the first four months of this year compared with a deficit of $607 million for the same period of last year, showed customs figures issued by state television on Tuesday.</p>
<p>		Jan-April 97	  Jan-April 96</p>
<p> EXPORTS     50.29		    39.629</p>
<p> IMPORTS     40.0		     40.237</p>
<p> BALANCE    +10.29		   - 0.607</p>
<p>Note: Figures in billions of U.S. dollars.  </p>
<p>Exports were up 26.9 percent compared with the first four months of last year, customs said.</p>
<p>Imports fell by 0.5 percent compared with the year-ago period, the figures showed.</p>
</text>
